post_install() {
    cat <<'NOTE'

==> OpenJiuwen Connect installed (channels + MCP server).

    The package installs:
        /usr/lib/openjiuwen-connect/venv/   — bundled virtualenv with adapter deps
        /usr/share/openjiuwen-connect/src/  — connect/ source tree
        /usr/bin/openjiuwen-channel-runner
        /usr/bin/openjiuwen-mcp-server
        /etc/openjiuwen-connect/            — your config goes here

    To enable the MCP server as a systemd unit (optional), create one like:

        [Unit]
        Description=OpenJiuwen MCP server
        After=network-online.target

        [Service]
        Type=simple
        ExecStart=/usr/bin/openjiuwen-mcp-server
        Restart=on-failure
        RestartSec=5

        [Install]
        WantedBy=multi-user.target

    The channel adapters need per-platform credentials (Telegram bot token,
    Slack app credentials, etc.). See connect/adapters/channels/README.md.

NOTE
}